From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:57:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the SD card pins at 1.8 V
 and 3.3 V

Bank PF of the A733 can run its pads from a 1.8 V or a 3.3 V supply,
which an SD card needs for UHS signalling. Add copies of the mmc0 pin
group that select the bank supply for either voltage.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the pin group for 1.8 V
is applied when the card runs at SDR104 (GPIO_POW_VAL_SET_CTL bit 0
reads 0), and the group for 3.3 V when a card came back in high-speed
mode (bit 0 reads 1).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 7c902f1ef1e6..a0c8fe89ff6a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -379,6 +379,26 @@ mmc0_pins: mmc0-pins {
 				bias-pull-up;
 			};
 
+			/* mmc0_pins with the bank PF supply for 1.8 V signalling */
+			mmc0_1v8_pins: mmc0-1v8-pins {
+				pins = "PF0", "PF1", "PF3", "PF4", "PF5";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "mmc0";
+				drive-strength = <10>;
+				bias-pull-up;
+				power-source = <1800000>;
+			};
+
+			/* mmc0_pins with the bank PF supply for 3.3 V signalling */
+			mmc0_3v3_pins: mmc0-3v3-pins {
+				pins = "PF0", "PF1", "PF3", "PF4", "PF5";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "mmc0";
+				drive-strength = <10>;
+				bias-pull-up;
+				power-source = <3300000>;
+			};
+
 			/* RST and CLK */
 			mmc2_clk_rst_pins: mmc2-clk-rst-pins {
 				pins = "PC1", "PC5";
